History and methods of Political-Economy (@history-and-methods-of-political-economy: 0, is #chapter, #outline) { r_695B2H52DHR8RZDZMZYPVT2KHE
This material follows changing economic and political questions through their theories, methods, institutions, and historical circumstances. Compare classical, Marxian, neoclassical, Keynesian, institutional, feminist, ecological, and other approaches through the problems they address and the claims they support. Routes introduce the selected history, formal model, statistical evidence, or interpretation before relying on it. Connect criticism and competing explanations with Philosophy, Sociology, and History rather than presenting a single school as the meaning of the whole field.

